# =============================================================================
# KarosL Frontend — Environment Configuration
# =============================================================================
# Copy this file to .env and adjust values for your environment.
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# Vite only exposes variables prefixed VITE_ to the browser bundle, and only
# reads them at BUILD time (not at container runtime) — see docs/DEVOPS.md.
# =============================================================================

# Base URL the SPA sends API requests to.
# Leave unset (or "/api") for the default: the Vite dev proxy (vite.config.js)
# and the Docker nginx reverse proxy (nginx.conf) both forward relative
# "/api/..." requests to the backend automatically — no localhost hardcoding.
# Only set this to an absolute URL (e.g. https://api.yourdomain.com/api) if
# the frontend and backend will be served from different origins.
# VITE_API_BASE_URL=/api

# --- AWS staging (single EC2 + Docker Compose) ---
# Leave this at the default "/api". Do NOT set it to http://<EC2_PUBLIC_IP>/api:
#   - the value is inlined into the JS bundle at BUILD time, so the EC2 IP
#     would be frozen into the image and every IP change would need a rebuild;
#   - it would turn same-origin calls into cross-origin ones, producing CORS
#     errors that the nginx reverse proxy otherwise makes impossible.
# On the server, only the root .env is used (docker-compose.yml passes
# VITE_API_BASE_URL in as a build arg). See docs/AWS_EC2_DEPLOYMENT.md §5.
